  <h2 id="story">When new pages left out their sources</h2>
  <p class="needs">Source: <a href={issue(241)}>Issue #241</a>, <a href={pull(249)}>PR #249</a>. One unattended run, 30 October 2026.</p>
  <p>One unattended run wrote the first Features, Examples and About pages of this site. The request asked that every example link the source files it changed. The review found that only one of five examples did; the fix took one short session, and the third round passed. The owner merged it the same evening.</p>
  <details class="proof">
    <summary>Records: the run step by step, figures, review rounds and the pull request</summary>
    <CaseSummary>
      <Fragment slot="changed">The first Features, Examples and About pages of this site.</Fragment>
      <Fragment slot="rounds">3. Round 1 raised one major finding, fixed in the same run; round 3 passed.</Fragment>
      <Fragment slot="found">That only one of the five examples linked the source files it changed, which an acceptance criterion required.</Fragment>
      <Fragment slot="result"><a href={pull(249)}>PR #249</a>, merged by the owner without a separate approval, 30 October, 20:09 UTC.</Fragment>
    </CaseSummary>
    <p class="lede">The Features, Examples and About pages of this site, now Why Codeyard, Projects and About, were first written by an agent, checked by a second agent from another provider, and corrected before the owner merged them. Nobody watched the run; the records it left tell the story.</p>
    <p>It started from <a href={issue(241)}>Issue #241</a>. Its acceptance criteria included this one: link every example to its Issue, its pull request and the source files it changed.</p>

    <figure class="plain">
      <svg class="lines" viewBox="0 0 1100 150" role="img" aria-labelledby="run-241-t" aria-describedby="run-241-words">
        <title id="run-241-t">The run of #241: implementation, round 1 and its fix, rounds 2 and 3, commit and pull request, and the merge by the owner.</title>
        <path class="l2" d="M70 60 H1030"/>
        <circle class="dot" cx="70" cy="60" r="10"/><text class="st" x="70" y="97" text-anchor="middle">Implement</text><text class="sub k" x="70" y="117" text-anchor="middle">19:27</text>
        <circle class="dot" cx="262" cy="60" r="10"/><text class="st" x="262" y="97" text-anchor="middle">Round 1</text><text class="sub k" x="262" y="117" text-anchor="middle">19:38</text>
        <circle class="dot" cx="454" cy="60" r="10"/><text class="st" x="454" y="97" text-anchor="middle">Fix</text><text class="sub k" x="454" y="117" text-anchor="middle">19:38</text>
        <circle class="dot" cx="646" cy="60" r="10"/><text class="st" x="646" y="97" text-anchor="middle">Rounds 2–3</text><text class="sub k" x="646" y="117" text-anchor="middle">19:40</text>
        <circle class="dot" cx="838" cy="60" r="10"/><text class="st" x="838" y="97" text-anchor="middle">Commit, PR</text><text class="sub k" x="838" y="117" text-anchor="middle">19:40</text>
        <rect class="gate" x="1020" y="50" width="20" height="20" transform="rotate(45 1030 60)"/><text class="st" x="1030" y="97" text-anchor="middle">Merge</text><text class="sub k" x="1030" y="117" text-anchor="middle">20:09</text>
      </svg>
    </figure>
    <ol class="words timeline" id="run-241-words">
      <li><b>The implementer built the pages</b><small class="k">19:27 – 19:38 UTC</small><p>The implementer, here Claude Opus, wrote the three pages and the styles in under eleven minutes, ran the project's checks, and wrote in its completion record that all six acceptance criteria were met.</p></li>
      <li><b>The independent reviewer found a gap</b><small class="k">19:38</small><p>The reviewer, here Codex, compared the pages with the Issue and found that only one of the five examples linked the source files it changed. It rated this major, and the triage confirmed it: fix now.</p></li>
      <li><b>The implementer fixed it, and the final review passed</b><small class="k">19:38 – 19:40</small><p>The implementer added the source files of the other four examples in 85 seconds. Round 2 reviewed only the fix and found nothing; round 3 reviewed the complete feature again and passed.</p></li>
      <li><b>The scripts opened a pull request</b><small class="k">19:40</small><p>Its description carries the evidence for each criterion, the checks and the review.</p></li>
      <li class="you"><b>The owner merged it</b><small class="k">20:09 UTC</small><p>No script merges. This change needed no separate approval, so the owner merged it like any pull request.</p></li>
    </ol>

    <h3>The figures</h3>
