  <h2 id="owner">When every feature got the same workflow</h2>
  <p class="needs">Source: <a href={issue(189)}>Issue #189</a>, <a href={pull(194)}>PR #194</a>, 27 October 2026.</p>
  <p>Nothing computed how risky a change was, so every feature went through the same steps, whatever it changed. The change computes a risk level from one policy file. Its three review rounds found nothing. The owner sharpened the scope in a comment and, before the merge, caught a defect: a failed listing of the changed files fell back to the default level instead of the highest.</p>
  <details class="proof">
    <summary>Records: figures, the owner's part and the changed files</summary>
    <CaseSummary>
      <Fragment slot="changed">The risk level of a feature is computed from one policy file.</Fragment>
      <Fragment slot="rounds">3, none with findings.</Fragment>
      <Fragment slot="found">Nothing. The owner found a defect before the merge: a failed listing of the changed files fell back to the default level.</Fragment>
      <Fragment slot="result"><a href={pull(194)}>PR #194</a>, merged by the owner with the required approval, 27 October, 14:47 UTC.</Fragment>
    </CaseSummary>
    <dl class="facts">
      <dt>tokens</dt><dd>about 3.2 million in all, about 730,000 of them for review. Source: the run record.</dd>
      <dt>interventions</dt><dd>1: the owner resumed the implementer by hand. Source: the run record.</dd>
      <dt>active run time</dt><dd>No single figure: the feature took four runs, because the owner resumed the implementer by hand. Source: the run record.</dd>
      <dt>total lead time</dt><dd>2 h 18 min, from the opening of the Issue, 12:29 UTC, to the merge; waiting and active time are not separated here. Source: the timestamps on GitHub.</dd>
    </dl>
    <p class="lede">Nothing in the workflow computed how risky a change was, so every feature went through the same steps, whatever it changed. #189 introduced the risk level, computed from one policy file. The owner sharpened its scope in a comment, and caught a defect before the merge.</p>
    <ul class="rules">
      <li><b>A comment as a decision.</b> After the first run, <a href={comment(189, "6443105170")}>the owner's comment</a> set two rules from experience with another project: an escalation reads only changed or removed lines of existing files, and a feature already in progress is not refused.</li>
      <li><b>A resumed session.</b> The owner resumed the implementer by hand, which the run record notes as an intervention. The record also shows the comment passed on to the resumed implementer and to each later review.</li>
      <li><b>A correction before the merge.</b> The owner found that a failed listing of the changed files fell back to the default level. The fix makes it high, with a test that fails against the earlier commit and passes with the fix, as the completion record in the pull request states.</li>
      <li><b>Three rounds, no findings.</b> Review by <code>codex gpt-6-luna</code>, ten of ten criteria met; full verifications of 556, 575 and 572 seconds.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Source files changed by <a href={pull(194)}>PR #194</a>: {changed[194].map((path, i) => (<>{i > 0 && ", "}<a href={repoFile(path)}><code>{path}</code></a></>))}.</p>
